WHY AGPL-3.0 AND NOT SOMETHING MORE PERMISSIVE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Two components BlockingBear depends on are themselves licensed under the
AGPL-3.0, and both are linked into the application rather than merely invoked as
external programs. A combined work that includes them can only be distributed
under the AGPL-3.0. This is not a preference; it is a condition inherited from
upstream:

  * PyMuPDF / MuPDF (Artifex Software) — imported throughout the document
    engine (app/engine/, see app/engine/mupdf_lock.py for the serialisation
    wrapper). Upstream states: "Dual Licensed - GNU AFFERO GPL 3.0 or Artifex
    Commercial License".

  * YOLO11n (Ultralytics) — app/engine/models/signature_yolo11n.onnx, the
    signature and stamp detector used by app/engine/image_ocr.py. Ultralytics
    licenses YOLO11 under AGPL-3.0 and takes the position that the licence
    extends to exported and derived weights.

Anyone wishing to redistribute BlockingBear under terms other than the
AGPL-3.0 must therefore first obtain commercial licences for these two
components from Artifex and Ultralytics respectively, or replace them.


